ination of transgranular and intergranular microcrack paths and a larger fracture edge area, indicating enhanced toughness, as well as widely spaced fatigue striations resulting from the relatively severe cyclic loading applied during the fatigue tests. Both parts of this research present a case study on 18Ni300M steel processed by PBF-LB, in which the atomization route played a decisive role in determining the microstructure and the mechanical properties, as revealed by tensile and rotary bending fatigue tests. The findings underscore the importance of refining the raw materials used in additive manufacturing and, based on that, defining post-processing strategies specifically tailored to control microstructural features, thereby enhancing performance.
